Still 1.2.0. A microphone meter on the pocket panel, with the threshold on it.

It draws the detector's own level — the phone's microphone, band-limited to the range a tap lives in and measured before anything else touches it. The mark on the track is what a tap has to reach, so you can see whether yours do instead of guessing. Shown while listening, which is when the phone is the microphone being tapped.

The three dots still fill as taps are counted.
